---
---
<section id="capacity-tradeoff" class="bg-background pt-16 pb-32">
  <div class="shell">
    <h2 class="display-lg text-center mx-auto max-w-4xl text-balance mb-6 leading-[1.1]">
      Build the capacity internally,<br/>
      or add it externally?
    </h2>
    <p class="text-center text-muted-foreground max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-16 text-[1.05rem]">
      Both can increase the capacity available to the business.<br/>
      They come with different commitments.
    </p>

    <div class="relative max-w-5xl mx-auto">
      <!-- Vertical dividing line -->
      <div class="absolute top-0 bottom-[-40px] left-1/2 w-px bg-hairline hidden md:block"></div>
      
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 border border-hairline bg-secondary/50">
        <!-- Left Side: Build Internally -->
        <div class="p-8 lg:p-16 relative group cursor-default transition-colors hover:bg-secondary/70">
          <div class="flex justify-center mb-12">
            <div class="eyebrow text-muted-foreground flex items-center gap-3">
              <span class="size-1.5 rounded-full bg-muted-foreground/40"></span>
              BUILD INTERNALLY
              <span class="size-1.5 rounded-full bg-muted-foreground/40"></span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <ul class="space-y-10 text-[0.95rem] text-muted-foreground">
            <li>Recruitment time and cost before capacity is available</li>
            <li>Salary and management overhead</li>
            <li>Reliance on individual hires</li>
            <li>Senior time spent managing operational finance</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Right Side: Add Calveris -->
        <div class="p-8 lg:p-16 bg-white relative shadow-[0_0_40px_rgba(0,0,0,0.03)] border-l border-hairline md:border-l-0 group cursor-default transition-all hover:shadow-[0_10px_50px_rgba(107,142,35,0.08)]">
          <div class="flex justify-center mb-12">
            <div class="eyebrow text-accent flex items-center gap-3">
              <span class="size-1.5 rounded-full bg-accent"></span>
              ADD CALVERIS
              <span class="size-1.5 rounded-full bg-accent"></span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <ul class="space-y-10 text-[0.95rem] text-foreground">
            <li>Capacity without starting a hiring cycle</li>
            <li>Capacity matched to the engagement</li>
            <li>Access to a wider delivery team</li>
            <li>Senior time available for higher-value work</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Connecting Box & Arrow below -->
      <div class="relative flex justify-center mt-10">
         <div class="w-px h-[40px] bg-hairline absolute top-[-40px]"></div>
         <div class="text-[#b1b8aa] mt-[-10px]">
           <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 0v14m0 0l-4-4m4 4l4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg>
         </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Bottom Text Section -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center mt-16">
      <div class="eyebrow text-muted-foreground/60 mb-8 tracking-[0.2em] text-[10px]">WHERE DO YOUR RESOURCES GO?</div>
      
      <h3 class="display-md mb-10 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        The real trade-off is where<br/>your resources end up.
      </h3>

      <div class="space-y-6 text-base text-muted-foreground mb-16">
        <p>Building internally commits money and management attention to building the function yourself.</p>
        <p class="text-foreground font-medium">Adding external capacity allows the required financial work to be handled while preserving more of those resources for the rest of the business.</p>
      </div>

      <a href="#build" class="eyebrow text-accent hover:text-accent-foreground transition-colors inline-flex items-center gap-3 group px-8 py-4 border border-accent/20 hover:bg-accent/5">
        SEE WHAT CALVERIS PROVIDES
        <span class="transition-transform duration-300 group-hover:translate-x-1">→</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
